      "block_preview_text": "Observe that farmers typically harvest in the early morning or late afternoon when cooler temperatures help maintain the asparagus's freshness. Highlight the process of selecting spears that reach about 20-25 centimeters in height with an appropriate thickness, cutting close to the base to avoid damaging the plant and allowing it to keep growing.",
